{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01204 - MONDO_18256",
  "verbalization": "Mitoxantrone, a chemotherapy agent, is linked to Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through its indication for Myeloid Leukemia and Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation, as well as its association with Acute Myeloid Leukemia Without Maturation. These relationships are supported by the indication chain involving Quizartinib, a drug that is indicated for AML with a T(8;16) translocation. The shared pathway through Quizartinib suggests a potential mechanism by which Mitoxantrone may influence the development or progression of AML with this specific translocation. The recurring use of Quizartinib as a bridge between Mitoxantrone and AML with T(8;16) translocation implies a possible role in the pathogenesis of this leukemia subtype. The evidence suggests that Mitoxantrone may exert some influence on the disease through its interaction with Quizartinib, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
